  "result": "Perfect! All 87 tests pass. Here's what I implemented:\n\n**VAT Calculation**\n\n1. **`src/invoices.js`** \u2014 Updated `invoiceTotals()` to calculate VAT:\n   - For each line: `lineTotal = qty \u00d7 unitPrice`\n   - For each line: `lineDiscount = roundCents(lineTotal \u00d7 discountPercent / 100)`\n   - For each line: `amountAfterDiscount = lineTotal - lineDiscount`\n   - For each line: `lineVAT = roundCents(amountAfterDiscount \u00d7 vatRate / 100)`\n   - `invoice.vat` = sum of all line VATs\n   - `invoice.total = subtotal - discount + vat` (clamped at 0)\n   - Returns `{ subtotal, discount, vat, total }`\n\n2. **`src/render.js`** \u2014 Updated `renderInvoiceText()` to show VAT:\n   - Displays VAT line (when > 0) just above the total\n   - Format: `VAT: \u20acX,XXX.XX`\n\n3. **Tests** \u2014 Added 6 new tests covering:\n   - VAT calculation on discounted amount\n   - Multiple lines with different VAT rates\n   - 0% VAT handling\n   - Per-line VAT rounding before summing\n   - Interaction of discount + VAT calculations\n\n4. **Updated 5 existing tests** to reflect VAT in totals:\n   - `invoiceTotals` tests now verify VAT included in total\n   - `renderInvoiceText` tests updated for VAT line in output\n\nAll 87 tests pass \u2713",
